# Netlify redirects.
#
# ## What changed when the routes became files
#
# This used to be an SPA catch-all — `/*  /index.html  200` — because the app
# was one empty document and react-router resolved everything from the URL. A
# hard load of /specimen/lucanus-cervus found no file, so the rule rewrote it to
# the shell and let the client work it out.
#
# Every route is now prerendered to its own file (`npm run prerender`), so the
# rewrite is no longer what serves a deep link — the file is. Netlify applies a
# redirect rule only when nothing on disk matches the request, unless the rule
# is *forced* with a `!`; this one is not, so `/calendar` is answered by
# `dist/calendar/index.html` and never reaches the line below.
#
# ## Why it points at 404.html and not index.html
#
# Because prerendering gave the shell contents. `/index.html` is no longer an
# empty div: it is the catalogue, fully rendered. Rewriting an unknown URL to it
# would show a visitor the catalogue for as long as it took the JavaScript to
# arrive, and then replace it with the not-found page — a flash of the wrong
# page that the old empty shell could not produce.
#
# `/404.html` is the same not-found page, prerendered. What the visitor sees
# statically is what the app renders once it hydrates, because react-router
# matches the URL that was actually asked for and lands on the same splat route.
# And the status is now true: an address the archive does not hold answers 404
# rather than 200, which is what it always meant.
#
# The safety net that has gone with it is real and worth stating: a route that
# exists in the router but is missing from `scripts/site-paths.ts` used to be
# served by the client anyway, and now 404s. That list is derived from the same
# directories the sitemap is built from, and `scripts/prerender/prerender.test.ts`
# holds it against the live route tree — which is a louder guarantee than the
# one it replaces.
#
# Last rule, and deliberately last: Netlify applies the first match, so any
# future proxy or redirect must go above this line.
/*  /404.html  404
